@startuml
title Architecture 5: Event-Driven Notification Pipeline
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam rectangle {
  BackgroundColor #FFFFFF
  BorderColor #1F4E79
}

package "Event Producers" {
  rectangle "Ride & Pool Service" as RideSvc
  rectangle "Join Service" as JoinSvc
  rectangle "Chat Service" as ChatSvc
}

rectangle "Event Bus / PubSub Stream" as EventBus

package "Notification Consumers" {
  rectangle "Live Push Controller\n(WebSocket Manager)" as PushCtrl
  rectangle "Email Fallback Service\n(For Offline Users)" as EmailSvc
}

node "Rider / Owner Client" {
  rectangle "Notification Center UI" as UI
}

RideSvc --> EventBus : Publish (Trip State Change, Seat Change)
JoinSvc --> EventBus : Publish (Request Accepted/Rejected/Drift)
ChatSvc --> EventBus : Publish (New Message)

EventBus --> PushCtrl : Consume Event
EventBus --> EmailSvc : Consume Critical Event (e.g., Ride Cancelled)

PushCtrl --> UI : Push Update (< 2s SLA)
EmailSvc --> UI : Email Delivery (If Client Disconnected)
@enduml